VMMLOG   TITLE 'CUCCA VM NETWORK MAILER VERSION 1 - VMM LOG EXIT'
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*      MAILER -- Copyright (c) 1982,1987 Columbia University.         *
*    Program Property of the Trustees of Columbia University in the   *
*    City of New York.                                                *
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
VMMLOG   CSECT ,
* VMMLOG -
*  This exit appends mail to a Columbia VMM-format log file (a VMMLOG)
*  which can be used to implement a "bulletin board."  This code is
*  a MAILER 1.24 rewrite of the older BBMAIL exit.
*
*  The name of the vmmlog file is derived from the rtparm field
*  for the filename,  "vmmlog" for the file type,  and the letter
*  specified in the mailer profile parm "<rtparm>-Mail-disk" or,
*  if not specified, "A".
*
* called via-
*  call vmmlog,(mailblok,actadr)
PAB      DSECT ,
@MBLOK   DS    A             ADDRESS OF MAILBLOK
@ACT     DS    A             ADDRESS OF ACTADR BLOCK
*
*---------------------------------------------------------------------*
*  How it works:
*   1) Find the current last record number in the VMMLOG.
*      a) If the file doesn't exist, initialize a new one.
*      b) If it does exist,  parse the preceding *:VmmE record for
*         the memo number.  Avoid decimal data exceptions :-)
*   2) Append a dummy *:VmmS header to the file.  The various header
*      item pointers or record count can't be filled in until we've
*      actually copied the mail file and looked for the headers.
*      (The header has a trailing ';' in column 80 to guarantee it is
*       of fixed length even though the file recfm is V.)
*   3) Copy the mail header (with rdhdr) to the file,  parsing for
*      the "Subject, From, To, Date, CC, Sender, Reply-To" fields.
*      Set the appropriate field header pointer in the in-core *:VmmS
*      header.
*   4) Copy the mail body (with rdtxt) to the file, counting records.
*   5) Now that the *:VmmS header has been filled in, fspoint back to
*      where the "place-holder" was written and rewrite the completed
*      header.
*   6) Make the necessary changes to the *:VmmS header to turn it into
*      a *:VmmE header and append it to the end of the file.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------*
         SPACE
* REGISTER USAGE -
R0  EQU  0 -
R1  EQU  1 -
R2  EQU  2 -
R3  EQU  3 -
R4  EQU  4 - work
R5  EQU  5 -
R6  EQU  6 -
R7  EQU  7 -
R8  EQU  8 - Record counter
R9  EQU  9 - VMMLOG file FSCB
R10 EQU 10 - The "current" VMM header/trailer buffer (base for VMMH)
R11 EQU 11 - MAILBLOK BASE
R12 EQU 12 - PROGRAM BASE
R13 EQU 13 - SAVE AREA
R14 EQU 14 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
R15 EQU 15 - SUBROUTINE LINKAGE
         SPACE
         PRINT NOGEN
         BLOCKS ,
         MAILBLOK ,
         FSTD  DSECT
         EJECT ,
VMMLOG   CSECT ,
         USING VMMLOG,R15    TEMPORARY ADDRESSABILITY
         B     EYESKIP       BRANCH OVER EYESKIP
MYNAME   DC    CL8'VMMLOG',CL8'&SYSDATE'
EYESKIP  DS    0H
         DROP  R15
         STM   R14,R12,12(R13) SAVE CALLER'S REGS
         LR    R12,R15       PERMANENT ADDRESSABILITY
         USING VMMLOG,R12
         LA    R14,SAVE      MY SAVE AREA
         ST    R13,4(R14)    SAVE CALLER'S PTR
         ST    R14,8(R13)    CHAIN MINE BACK
         LR    R13,R14       SET MY SAVE PTR
         USING PAB,R1        ADDRESS THE PARMS
         L     R11,@MBLOK    GET MAILBLOK BASE
         USING MAILBLOK,R11  make use of it
         L     R1,@ACT       GET ACTADR ADDRESS
         USING ACTADR,R1     ADDRESS IT
         L     R1,ACTRT      GET ROUTD ADDRESS
         USING ROUTD,R1      ADDRESS IS
         MVC   FNAME,RTPARM  USE PARM AS FILE NAME
         DROP  R1            done with ROUTD
         CLI   FNAME,C' '    did they provide a filename?
         BNE   FNAMEOK       -> the name filled in is OK.
         MVC   FNAME,=CL8'BBOARD' else default it to BBOARD.
FNAMEOK  EQU   *             <- here when name is set
         SPACE ,
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*   FIND FILEMODE OF VMMLOG DISK
*   THIS DEFAULT TO "A6" BUT CAN BE OVERIDDEN BY A PARM KEYWORD
*   COMPOSED OF THE RTPARM (OR FILE) NAME AND "-MAIL-DISK".  FOR
*   EXAMPLE:
*        US-MAIL-DISK=F
*        SY-MAIL-DISK=G
*        SYSTEM-MAIL-DISK=H
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         LA    R1,FNAME+8    POINT TO END OF NAME
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',X'FF' TRAP ON BLANKS
         TRT   FNAME,TRAPTAB TRAP THE FIRST BLANK
         MVI   TRAPTAB+C' ',X'00' RESET THE TABLE
         S     R1,=A(FNAME)  GET LENGTH OF TOKEN
         BCTR  R1,0          -1 FOR EXECUTE
         EX    R1,MOVER      MVC PARMDISK(0),FNAME
         LA    R2,PARMDISK+1(R1) GET POSITION TO COPY FIXED PART FROM
         MVC   0(L'MAILDISK,R2),MAILDISK BUILD THE PARM NAME
         MVC   FMODE,=CL2'A6'  DEFAULT SETTING
         LA    R3,L'MAILDISK+1(R1) GET LENGTH OF PARM NAME
         L     R5,MAILPTAB   GET MAILER PARM TABLE
         L     R15,ATBLUK
         CALL  (15),((R5),PARMDISK,(R3),TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       FIND IT
         BNZ   NODISK        NOPE
         CLI   0(R1),1       1 CHARACTER OR 2?
         BH    NDISK1        2
         MVC   FMODE(1),1(R1) GET THE FIRST LETTER, NUMBER IS 2
         B     NODISK
NDISK1   EQU   *
         MVC   FMODE,1(R1)   GET LETTER AND NUMBER (I.E. F2)
NODISK   EQU   *
         SPACE ,
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* 0) Initialize the *:VmmS and *:VmmE buffers.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         MVI   VMMS,C' '     start with a blank
         MVC   VMMS+1(L'VMMS-1),VMMS and then propagate it.
         USING VMMH,R10      R10 will always point at *some* VMM header
         LA    R10,VMMS      first grab the header.
         MVC   VMMIDENT,=C'*:VmmS' initalize
         MVI   VMMLAST,C';'  drop off the trailing semicolon
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*  1) Find record number we will be appending at....
*     a) State the file and create it if it doesn't exist.
*     b) For an existing file, read the last record which should
*        be a VmmE.  Parse out the memo number and increment it.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         LA    R3,FNAME
         FSSTATE (R3),ERROR=FSSERR,FORM=E
         USING FSTD,R1
         L     R4,FSTAIC               get record count
         DROP  R1
         FSREAD (R3),RECNO=(R4),BUFFER=PREVHDR,RECFM=V,BSIZE=80,       *
               ERROR=FSRERR,FORM=E
         LR    R9,R1                   get fscb
         FSCLOSE FSCB=(R9)             close it (in case of CDF)
         LA    R4,1(,R4)               +1 is where the new VmmS goes.
         ST    R4,RECNO                save for later
         LA    R10,PREVHDR             look at previous header
         CLC   =C'*:Vmm',VMMIDENT      see if it is proper data.
         BNE   CORRUPT                 -> file has become corrupted
         CLI   VMMHLINS,C'='           memo # is preceeded by '='
         BNE   CORRUPT                 -> junk
         TRT   VMMHLINS+1(L'VMMHLINS-1),DIGITS look for non-decimal
         BNZ   CORRUPT                 -> avoid decimal data exceptions
         PACK  DWORD,VMMHLINS+1(L'VMMHLINS-1)  good ole PD
         AP    DWORD,=P'1'             add 1 to the current seqnum
         UNPK  NEXTSEQ,DWORD           to get the new one
         OI    NEXTSEQ+L'NEXTSEQ-1,X'F0'
CREATED  EQU   *                       <- "come from" FSSERR/CREATE
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
*   Fill in the VmmS fields that we know about now.
*--------------------------------------------------------------------
         LA    R10,VMMS      repoint VMMH base at *:VmmS buffer
         MVC   VMMKEY,=CL8' ' SET DEFAULT KEY TO BLANKS
         LA    R1,TDATE      4 DWORDS
         DC    X'8310000C'   GET TIME
         MVC   VMMDATEN(2),TDATE+6 GET YEAR PAIR
         MVC   VMMDATEN+2(2),TDATE GET MONTH PAIR
         MVC   VMMDATEN+4(2),TDATE+3 GET DAY PAIR
         MVC   VMMTIMEN(2),TDATE+8   GET TIMESTAMP
         MVC   VMMTIMEN+2(2),TDATE+11
         MVC   VMMTIMEN+4(2),TDATE+14
         L     R5,MAILKTAB   GET MAIL FILE KEYWORD TABLE
         L     R15,ATBLUK
         CALL  (15),((R5),KEYWORD,L'KEYWORD,TWORK)
         LTR   R15,R15       FIND IT
         BNZ   NOKEY         NOPE
         LR    R6,R1         COPY FIELDD POINTER
         USING FIELDD,R6     ADDRESS IT
         ICM   R6,B'1111',FITOK GET TOKEN LIST
         DROP  R6
         USING TOKEND,R6     THIS IS THE "KEYWORD:" TOKEN
         ICM   R6,B'1111',TOKNEXT  NEXT IS THE KEYWORD VALUE
         BZ    NOKEY         NO KEYWORD SUPPLIED
         SR    R4,R4         GET ZERO
         MVC   VMMKEY,=CL8' '  BLANK IT
         L     R4,TOKLEN     GET LENGTH
         C     R4,=F'8'      CHECK LENGTH
         BNH   *+8           TRUNCATE IF MORE THAN 8
         LA    R4,8
         L     R6,TOKPTR          STRING POINTER
         DROP  R6
         BCTR  R4,0          -1 FOR EXECUTE
         EX    R4,MOVEKEY    MOVE THE KEYWORD IN
         OC    VMMKEY,=CL8' ' CONVERT TO UPPER CASE
NOKEY    EQU   *
* append the partially filled in VmmS record.  Come back to it later.
         FSWRITE FSCB=(R9),BUFFER=VMMS,RECFM=V,BSIZE=80,               *
               RECNO=0,ERROR=FSWERR,FORM=E
*---------------------------------------------------------------------
* 3) Write the mail header out to the file now.  As each header line
*    is written:
*    a) keep track of the number of records written
*    b) look for the keywords and if found plug the record number into
*       the VmmS header.
*---------------------------------------------------------------------
         LA    R8,1          currently have written one record out.
HDRLOOP  EQU   *             <- top of header copying loop
         LA    R1,L'BUFFER   set max buffer length for RDHDR
         ST    R1,BUFLEN      "   "   "       "     "    "
         L     R15,ARDHDR    address of the header reader
         CALL  (15),(BUFFER,BUFLEN) call rdhdr; buflen gets updated
         LTR   R15,R15       end of header?
         BNZ   HDREND        end of the header loop
         L     R4,BUFLEN     get length of this header line
         FSWRITE FSCB=(R9),BUFFER=BUFFER,RECFM=V,BSIZE=(R4),           *
               ERROR=FSWERR,FORM=E
         LA    R8,1(,R8)     increment record counter
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Check for header keywords:  Uppercase the buffer and then compare
*  the list of keywords.  The list is pretty small,  so just do it
*  inline instead of mucking around with some sort of table.
*  Also,  it's pretty safe to ignore the length of the buffer.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         TR    BUFFER,UPCASE upper case the buffer
         CLC   =C'SUBJECT',BUFFER
         BE    HDRSUBJ
         CLC   =C'FROM',BUFFER
         BE    HDRFROM
         CLC   =C'TO',BUFFER
         BE    HDRTO
         CLC   =C'DATE',BUFFER
         BE    HDRDATE
         CLC   =C'CC',BUFFER
         BE    HDRCC
         CLC   =C'SENDER',BUFFER
         BE    HDRSEND
         CLC   =C'REPLY-TO',BUFFER
         BE    HDRREPL
* Not one of the keywords, so just get the next header line
         B     HDRLOOP
HDRSUBJ  LA    R3,VMMSUBJ    point to field to fill in
         B     HDRCOMM       and go do common code
HDRFROM  LA    R3,VMMFROM
         B     HDRCOMM
HDRTO    LA    R3,VMMTO
         B     HDRCOMM
HDRDATE  LA    R3,VMMDATE
         B     HDRCOMM
HDRCC    LA    R3,VMMCC
         B     HDRCOMM
HDRSEND  LA    R3,VMMSENDR
         B     HDRCOMM
HDRREPL  LA    R3,VMMREPTO
HDRCOMM  EQU   *             <- common code for header record numbers
         CVD   R8,DWORD      convert record number to decimal
         SP    DWORD,=P'1'   minus 1 (don't count VmmS line)
         UNPK  0(5,R3),DWORD unpack into appropriate header field
         OI    4(R3),X'F0' fix the zone
         B     HDRLOOP       -> get next header line
HDREND   EQU   *             <- here when end of hdr
         CVD   R8,DWORD      put the number of header lines in VmmS
         UNPK  VMMHLINS,DWORD
         OI    VMMHLINS+L'VMMHLINS-1,X'F0'
* Drop off a blank line to seperate header from body
         FSWRITE FSCB=(R9),BUFFER=ONEBLANK,RECFM=V,BSIZE=1,            *
               ERROR=FSWERR,FORM=E
         LA    R8,1(,R8)     increment record count
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* 4) Copy message body to the file.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
TXTLOOP  EQU   *             <- top of body copying loop
         LA    R1,L'BUFFER   set max buffer length for RDTXT
         ST    R1,BUFLEN      "   "   "       "     "    "
         L     R15,ARDTXT    address of the text reader
         CALL  (15),(BUFFER,BUFLEN) call rdtxt; buflen gets updated
         LTR   R15,R15       end of text?
         BNZ   TXTEND        -> end of the text part
         L     R4,BUFLEN     length of this line
         FSWRITE FSCB=(R9),BUFFER=BUFFER,RECFM=V,BSIZE=(R4),           *
               ERROR=FSWERR,FORM=E
         LA    R8,1(,R8)     increment record counter
         B     TXTLOOP       -> back to the top
TXTEND   EQU   *             <- end of the text
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
* 5) Finish filling in the header/trailer with the record count in R8.
*    Write out the trailer record and rewrite the header record.
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         CVD   R8,DWORD      put the total number of lines in VmmS
         UNPK  VMMLINES,DWORD
         OI    VMMLINES+L'VMMLINES-1,X'F0'
         MVC   VMME,VMMS     now dup the header into the trailer
         LA    R10,VMME      point at the trailer buffer
         MVI   VMMIDENT+5,C'E'   change VmmS to VmmE
         MVI   VMMHLINS,C'=' prepend '=' to message number
         MVC   VMMHLINS+1(4),NEXTSEQ   copy sequence number in
         FSWRITE FSCB=(R9),BUFFER=VMME,RECFM=V,BSIZE=80,ERROR=FSWERR,  *
               FORM=E
         L     R4,RECNO      remember recnum of VmmS
         FSWRITE FSCB=(R9),BUFFER=VMMS,RECFM=V,BSIZE=80,ERROR=FSWERR,  *
               FORM=E,RECNO=(R4) rewrite the completed VmmS header
         FSCLOSE FSCB=(R9)   close it
         LOG   VMM066,(CA,FNAME)
         SR    R15,R15
RET      EQU   *
         L     R13,4(R13)              GET CALLER'S SAVE PTR
         L     R14,12(R13)             GET R14
         LM    R0,R12,20(R13)          GET R0-R12
         BR    R14                     RETURN
         SPACE ,
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
*  Error junk
*----------------------------------------------------------------------
         SPACE ,
CORRUPT  DS    0H           <- here when VMMLOG is full of garbage
         LOG   VMM065,(CA,FNAME)
         LA    R15,8
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
FSSERR   DS    0H           <- here for FSSTATE error.
         C     R15,=F'28'   if file not found
         BE    CREATE       -> create it
         LA    R4,=CL8'FSSTATE'
         B     FSCOMMON     -> go to common code
CREATE   EQU   *            <- here to initialize new file
         FSWRITE (R3),BUFFER=ONEBLANK,RECFM=V,BSIZE=1,FORM=E,          *
               ERROR=FSWERR
         MVC   RECNO,=F'2'  where new VmmS gets written
         MVC   NEXTSEQ,=CL4'0001' new message sequence number
         LR    R9,R1        address of FSCB
         B     CREATED      -> new file created.
         SPACE ,
FSRERR   DS    0H           <- here for FSREAD error.
         LA    R4,=CL8'FSREAD'
         B     FSCOMMON     -> go to the common code
         SPACE ,
FSWERR   DS    0H           <- here for FSWRITE error.
         LA    R4,=CL8'FSWRITE'
         B     FSCOMMON     -> go to the common code
         SPACE ,
FSCOMMON DS    0H           <- common code for FS errors
         LR    R5,R15       preserve return code
         LOG   VMM050,(CA,(R4),D,(R5))
         LR    R15,R5
         B     RET
         SPACE ,
MOVEKEY  MVC   VMMKEY(0),0(R6)
MOVER    MVC   PARMDISK(0),FNAME
DIGITS   DC    256X'1'                 xlate table to find bad numbers
         ORG   DIGITS+C'0'
         DC    10X'0'
         ORG   DIGITS+C' '   blank is like zero
         DC    X'0'
         ORG   ,
         LTORG ,
ONEBLANK DC    C' '          like the name says
KEYWORD  DC    C'KEYWORDS'
MAILDISK DC    C'-MAIL-DISK' RIGHT END OF "<PARM>-MAIL-DISK"
FNAME    DC    CL8'SYSTEM',CL8'VMMLOG'
FMODE    DS    CL2           SYSTEM MAIL FILE DISK
SAVE     DS    18F                     SAVE AREA
DWORD    DS    D
TWORK    DS    32D
TDATE    DS    4D
RECNO    DS    F
NEXTSEQ  DS    CL4
BUFFER   DC    CL80' '
BUFLEN   DS    F
PARMDISK DC    C'12345678-MAIL-DISK'  MAX LENGTH PARAMETER NAME
VMMS     DS    CL80          the *:VmmS header
VMME     DS    CL80          the *:VmmE trailer
PREVHDR  DS    CL80          the previous *:VmmE trailer
VMMH     DSECT ,             The VMM header/trailer
         COPY  VMM
         END   VMMLOG
